portunity um you  know to really move this more squarely  this discussion more squarely into the  public forum um and you know i think if  you go back a couple of years um you  know i think there was a general sense  in the industry hey nothing's going to  get done on capitol hill we have to deal  with the agencies i think maybe that's  changed i think maybe what they see is  now um the best opportunity for you know  achieving um you know some degree of  movement um in this space is going to  come from capitol hill and so i think  that's a big part of  this but look this is a very very  important hearing for the industry there  are a lot of really big topics being  covered here so um i think that they  feel the um you know the gravity the  gravity of this of this movement i  should say  is your view that the big crypto stars  here want regulation they just want it  to be done correctly  so i think um  what  there is a a clear understanding in the  space that the idea that um all of this  is going to stay sort of you know in  this sort of dark unregulated um you  know realm  that's just not the reality um you know  i think that that's they recognize that  and that's a big part of what they're  doing now they certainly look at  regulation as being a double-edged sword  it it stimulates adoption on the one  hand um but done wrong you know  incorrectly it can it can really stifle  innovation and and stifle adoption of  the technology so i think the short  answer is yes but with uh with an  asterisk right we just heard one of the  lawmakers who used to work in it saying  that uh if they had thwarted dial up  back in the day and innovation with the  internet we would we would still be  working with dial up i think that's a  really astute comparison there you know  what's the worst case scenario here for  people who work in the crypto industry  like yourselves what are you hoping to  not have happen today  yeah so we you know we we actually began  life focusing on on um yo